{"id": 14003, "group": "campus-iit-gandhinagar-placements", "sent_at": "2026-10-27T06:06:15.323747+00:00", "text": "Eternal Sde:\n\n1) CF 1324F\n2) LC 924\n3)\n Given two arrays a and b \nFor each element in a (a[i]), you have to find the index (1 - based) of an element in array b  (b[j]) such that b[j] > a[i] and if there are multiple as such then return the minimum index one \nYou have to return the vector of indices\n\nEternal PA role:\n\nThree sections\n\n20 mcqs \n\nSecond section was 3 sql questions  \nFirst and second question were  cities having more customers than average and duplicate bid detection\n\nThird question: \nTwo tables were given one anonymous viewers one for subscribed viewers and their login and exit timestamps were given we had to output two rows one for annonymous, count of their viewers and average total seconds spent online and same for subscribed\n\nthe third section was 4 python mcqs\n\nIITG", "author_tag": "IITG", "reply_to": null, "attachment": null, "deleted": false}
